package agentsdoc

import "strings"

// writeV04dInlineSection documents inline mode for an authoring agent: the
// region, `--inline` on dump, inspect, play, and run, the commit: step and
// the scrollback member, and what a host's Commit prints. It names no path of
// the repository, since the project briefing (ProjectMarkdown) is this same
// text.
func writeV04dInlineSection(b *strings.Builder) {
	b.WriteString("### v0.4d: inline mode\n\n")
	b.WriteString("- Inline mode draws the active screen as a live region below the terminal's cursor, instead of in the alternate screen, and the host prints into the terminal's own scrollback above it with `Commit`. The host chooses it, for a `<tui>` without `version` only: `RunWith(ctx, w, RunOptions{Inline: true})` in Go, `--inline` on `tuimark run`. For a document that writes `version` it is the error `tuimark: inline mode needs a <tui> without version` (`tuimark: dump: …`, `tuimark: play: …`, `tuimark: run: …` on the command line), before the terminal is touched. It is a way to run a document, not vocabulary: nothing in the markup changes.\n")
	b.WriteString("- The region is the active screen laid out at the terminal's width and at the height of its content, as a modal sized by its content is: a `col` or `row` child of the screen is `1fr` and takes what the other children leave, and a `%` height is `L002`. A `height` or `max-height` in cells on the screen caps it, a `min-height` in cells raises it, never past the terminal's rows; the built-in `height: 100%` of `screen` does not apply. `@media` reads the terminal's columns and rows, never the region's. The region follows its content: it grows when a node appears and shrinks when it goes. Content taller than the terminal is cut at the region's end (`L009`), shared as a modal's children share its cap: an `fr` child and a `scroll`, `list`, or `table` take what the others leave, so a transcript in a `<scroll stick=\"bottom\">` shows its end with the composer and the status in view, and one in a `box` pushes them out. A modal and an open option list are laid out against the region as against a screen of its size, and the region does not grow for them. The document's `mouse` is ignored: an inline session has no mouse.\n")
	b.WriteString("- `tuimark dump FILE --inline`, `inspect FILE --inline`, and `play FILE --inline` lay the screen out as the region, with `--rows` as the terminal's rows: the dump's `rows` and its `grid` are the region's, and `terminal_rows`, right after `rows`, is `--rows`. `tuimark_dump`, `tuimark_inspect`, and `tuimark_play` take `inline`, and a golden manifest entry takes `\"inline\": true`.\n")
	b.WriteString("- `Commit` prints rows above the region: `Commit{Lines: …}`, each line a string or an array of runs (runs, normalized as run text; an LF starts a new row; a line is wrapped at the terminal's width with `pre-wrap`), or `Commit{Template, With, Props}`, the copy of a `<template>` built as a `<use>` without `id` at the root of the active screen: its ids are dropped, its `<slot/>` is empty, its paths are read once, and it is laid out from column 0 at the terminal's width with the height of its content. A committed line is styled by the document's cascade as a child of the active screen (`text` and `screen > text` rules, and the spans of its runs); the screen's padding, border, and background are not part of it. A card whose content comes through its slot is committed through a wrapper template that has no slot: write the item to a scratch path, commit the wrapper with `with`, and clear the path. A commit that fails prints nothing: `commit: give either lines or template`, `commit: with and props need a template`, `commit: line N is TYPE, not a string or an array of runs`, `commit: no <template id=\"T\">`, `commit: with path \"P\" (alias A) is missing`, `commit: prop \"P\" is not declared by <template id=\"T\">`, and, outside an inline session, `commit: not in inline mode`.\n")
	b.WriteString("- `tuimark play FILE --inline` takes the step `commit:JSON` (`{\"commit\": {\"lines\": [\"a\"]}}` in a `--script`; the JSON of a `commit:` step has no spaces in `--input`), prints the committed rows in `scrollback` after `events` (`{\"grid\", \"styles\"}`, each row the terminal's width, `styles` only with `--styles`; an `=== scrollback ===` section in the text form), and with `--frames` each frame has `scrollback_rows`, the rows committed up to its step. A failed commit is the usage error `tuimark: play: step N (STEP): REASON`. To check an inline screen, replay it: commit what the host would, and read `scrollback` and the region's `grid`.\n")
	b.WriteString("- What `Run()` writes: no `CSI ? 1049 h`, `CSI H`, or `CSI 2 J`; rows are reached with `CR`, `CSI N A`, and `CSI N B`, columns with `CSI n G`, new rows by `CR LF`, and the rows the region no longer uses are erased with `CSI J`. A commit moves to the region's first row, erases, writes its rows (cells to the last one that is not blank, `CSI 0 m CR LF`), and draws the region again. A new size erases the region and draws it again; rows already committed belong to the terminal and are never repainted. On every exit path the region is erased and the cursor is left at the start of its first row, after the rows committed before the end. `TUIMARK_LOG`'s `start` record has `\"inline\": true`, and a `commit` record has `line_count` and `rows`, never the text.\n\n")
}
